  "summary": "Five new reports show distinct stress-triggered quality-control routes acting on organelle contacts, peroxisomes, lysosomes, endosomes and extracellular proteins.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is stress-responsive organelle and proteostasis remodeling, largely through selective autophagy and its regulators. Preprints describe Contact-phagy, in which SIGMAR1-CCPG1 turns over ER-mitochondria contact-site subdomains, and sortilin as an extracellular scavenger receptor for leaked non-glycosylated cytosolic proteins bearing hydrophobic patches. Published work links iron deficiency to pexophagy via a GABARAP-FLCN/FNIP1 interaction that activates TFEB and TFE3, shows processing bodies forming with stress granules during recovery from lysosomal damage to support lysosomal quality and survival, and places RAB11-RAB30 on endosomes under starvation, shear and osmotic stress, using phosphoinositide turnover to drive autophagy. The items span different compartments rather than a single mechanism; what is new is the identification of specific adaptors, receptors and condensates tied to each stress context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
